{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1490786-gangrel-1st-edition-weakness","id":1490786,"title":"Gangrel 1st Edition Weakness","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-20T07:00:30-07:00","id":1490786,"title":"Gangrel 1st Edition Weakness","content":"Hey all, I'm going to be playing in a slightly modified game of first edition Requiem and was considering Gangrel for a character. My experience is only with 2nd and the weaknesses are obviously very different. My background was going to include some pretty heavy mental focus but I was concerned about the potential penalties to Int and Wits. Does the weakness play mechanically as super hard to rolls? Does overly stocking up on mental skills, attributes make enough of a difference? I know there is WP to spend but it isn't something I'd want to do for every roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27502-caelican","name":"Caelican","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-20T13:57:41-07:00","id":1490810,"title":"","content":"How bad it is really comes down to how often you're rolling, and how often you need multiple successes.<br /> <br /> If you're focused on Mental stuff, but generally only looking at simple actions that you only need 1 success for, you'll be fine despite the weakness; especially with plenty of dice.<br /> <br /> If you end up doing a lot of extended actions, or rolls that require multiple successes (included contested rolls) it hits a lot harder.<br /> <br /> Something else to consider is talking to your ST about how they intend to handle X-again bonuses and penalized rolls such as the Gangrel Weakness. There's a few fairly low level Merits that grant you 9-again on rolls with a specific Skill. The books don't have much of an official way to handle this. So STs will have the worst modifier apply, some the best, and some create a scaling system, etc. If your ST is on the generous side here, it's not hard to have a few Skills you can be good at despite the weakness even if all of them would be a big investment of XP and in-character time.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-22T13:12:47-07:00","id":1491033,"title":"","content":"Honestly, we're using the 2nd ed weakness for our 1st ed game for Gangrel. It's much better. I'd try arguing that way first.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27553-salarion","name":"Salarion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}